# Lodestar — environment template. Copy to `.env` and edit:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Three things to know before you rely on this file:
#
#   1. **Who actually reads it differs, and the difference bites.** Docker
#      Compose reads it. The *brain* does not: run it natively and it takes the
#      defaults below, not this file, so export it yourself first —
#          set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#      The *RAG lab* is the exception: it reads repo-root `.env` on its own
#      (`load_env_file`, brain/tests/raglab/config.py), because the lab is
#      started by hand and would otherwise need the export every time.
#   2. **An empty value is not "no value".** For the two model knobs, empty means
#      "whatever the chosen backend serves" — see BRAIN_MODEL below. Everything
#      else commented out here is genuinely the code's own default.
#   3. Running the brain natively also needs `BRAIN_URL_SAFETY=off` unless you
#      have a Safe Browsing key: the default refuses to boot without one, by
#      design. Compose already pins `off` for this reason.
#
# The defaults are deliberately local, free and offline-capable: a model on this
# machine via Ollama, a Persian-tuned embedder downloaded on first retrieval. You
# need no key to run the board, and no key to run the Assistant against Ollama.
# Full reference, with what each backend costs and what it can do: README.md.


# ── Keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed for the hosted routes. The local defaults never read them, and the
# browser never sees them — the Node server proxies to the brain, which is the
# only process that holds a credential.

# Remote LLM access. Required only when BRAIN_LLM=openrouter (or when the
# Assistant's model picker is switched to a hosted model), and for the judged
# half of the RAG lab.
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works, which is what lets Ollama and OpenRouter
# share one construction site in `llm.py` instead of two.
#OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# Link checking for web-search results. `BRAIN_URL_SAFETY=google-safe-browsing`
# refuses to boot without it, on purpose — a link checker that silently passes
# everything is worse than none. Compose therefore pins `off` so a keyless
# `docker compose up` still works.
#GOOGLE_SAFE_BROWSING_KEY=


# ── Chat model ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `ollama` = a model on this machine: free, private, no key. `openrouter` = a
# hosted model, needs the key above. `fake` = deterministic canned replies, for
# tests. An unknown value raises at boot rather than falling back to something
# you did not ask for.
#BRAIN_LLM=ollama
# Empty does NOT mean "no model" — choosing the backend chooses the model, via
# PROVIDER_MODELS (config.py): openrouter -> openai/gpt-5-nano,
# ollama -> 4skl/gemma4-e2b-mtp, fake -> openai/gpt-5-nano. Leaving this empty is
# the safe setting; a remote slug left standing under `ollama` would make every
# run refuse for a model you never picked. Name one only to override, and then
# the row's label and the model that produced it must agree.
#BRAIN_MODEL=
#BRAIN_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# If BRAIN_LLM=ollama and the daemon is down, every chat answers with a
# connection error. `ollama serve` first, or switch to openrouter/fake.


# ── Embeddings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The default model is Persian-tuned because this board's diary corpus is Farsi:
# an English-only embedder returns confident numbers that measure nothing on it.
# ~2.2 GB, downloaded on **first retrieval, not boot**, so /health keeps
# answering while it fetches. `fastembed` is a smaller ONNX list; `fake` is the
# offline test backend. Needs the `local-embeddings` extra.
#BRAIN_EMBEDDER=sentence-transformers
#BRAIN_EMBED_MODEL=


# ── Retrieval gate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The relevance gate between retrieval and generation — the measured choice for
# this corpus (candidate F). `none` disables it; `lexical` needs no model.
#BRAIN_GRADER=llm
#BRAIN_GRADE_THRESHOLD=0.4


# ── Chat memory (Chroma) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The project's own Chroma container: `npm run chroma` (:8003), test twin
# `npm run chroma-test` (:8004). Real and test data never share a store.
# `memory` runs Chroma in-process with no container and no disk, for tests.
#BRAIN_CHROMA_URL=http://localhost:8003
# Derived from BOARD_API_URL when unset, which is what keeps the :3000 board and
# the :3001 sandbox from writing into each other's collections.
#BRAIN_CHROMA_DATABASE=
#BRAIN_CHAT_COLLECTION=


# ── Voice input ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `parakeet` transcribes locally: free, private, Apple Silicon only, 2.5 GB on
# first use. Compose pins `openrouter` because the image cannot install mlx.
# `fake` is the offline test backend. No `auto` mode — one config must not
# transcribe privately on one machine and bill an API on another.
#BRAIN_TRANSCRIBER=parakeet
#BRAIN_PARAKEET_MODEL=mlx-community/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3
#BRAIN_OMNI_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite


# ── Web-result safety ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# See GOOGLE_SAFE_BROWSING_KEY above. `off` skips the check; `fake` is scripted
# for tests. Deliberately not a keyword screen on the query — this board holds a
# private life, and "unlawful eviction, what are my rights" is a question it
# exists to answer.
#BRAIN_URL_SAFETY=google-safe-browsing


# ── Wiring ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which board the brain writes to. Boards pair with brains by last digit:
# :3000 board <-> :9000 brain, :3001 sandbox <-> :9001 brain.
#BOARD_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
#BRAIN_MAX_STEPS=8


# ── Node server: rate limit and backups ──────────────────────────────────────
# One token bucket over the whole assistant surface (/api/agent/*, /api/rag/*).
# The board API is never metered: being over the assistant's limit must not make
# your own cards unreachable.
#LODESTAR_AGENT_BURST=60
#LODESTAR_AGENT_PER_MIN=240

# Every test entry point backs up board.db first, and a save carrying never-seen
# cards snapshots too. Test harnesses set LODESTAR_BACKUP_ON_WRITE=0 so test
# boards cannot evict real snapshots. Google Drive upload is opt-in via rclone
# (one-time OAuth; no Google password is ever stored or read) and a missing
# rclone warns rather than blocking.
#LODESTAR_BACKUP_ON_WRITE=1
#LODESTAR_BACKUP_DIR=backups
#LODESTAR_BACKUP_KEEP=100
#LODESTAR_RCLONE_BIN=rclone
# The rclone *remote name* only — the destination path is added by the script, so
# this is `gdrive`, not `gdrive:lodestar-backups`.
#LODESTAR_RCLONE_REMOTE=gdrive


# ── RAG lab (test-only, :9002 / Inspector :9003) ─────────────────────────────
# Nothing in production reads these. The lab keeps no database and deliberately
# ignores BRAIN_CHROMA_URL: an experiment must not find the board's store just
# because it happens to be running.
#RAGLAB_LLM=ollama
# Same PROVIDER_MODELS rule as BRAIN_MODEL above, same table.
#RAGLAB_MODEL=
#RAGLAB_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# The fastembed backend's default checkpoint. Multilingual on purpose — this one
# has a real default, unlike the model knobs above.
#RAGLAB_FASTEMBED_MODEL=sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2
# Multilingual too: fastembed's own default rerankers are English-only and score
# Farsi pairs as noise.
#RAGLAB_CROSS_ENCODER=jinaai/jina-reranker-v2-base-multilingual
# The sweep's answerer and judge are different models on purpose — a model
# grading its own output is not evidence, and that pairing is refused rather than
# trusted. Both default per backend from PAIRINGS (sweep.py), keyed on RAGLAB_LLM:
#   openrouter -> answerer openai/gpt-5-nano,   judge openai/gpt-5-mini
#   ollama     -> answerer 4skl/gemma4-e2b-mtp, judge gemma4:e2b
# Override only to name two models the active backend actually serves, and screen
# the judge first (`npm run raglab:judgescreen`) — picking the judge after seeing
# the leaderboard it produces is judge-shopping, and with a candidate field
# spanning ~0.01 it is effortless to do by accident.
#RAGLAB_SWEEP_ANSWER_MODEL=
#RAGLAB_SWEEP_JUDGE_MODEL=


# ── Fully offline (tests, CI) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BRAIN_LLM=fake BRAIN_EMBEDDER=fake BRAIN_CHROMA_URL=memory BRAIN_URL_SAFETY=fake


# ── The setup this project is actually developed against ─────────────────────
# A hosted chat model for the Assistant, a local one for the lab — the lab's
# sweeps are k model calls per question, which is the bill no OpenRouter credit
# survives, and running them locally is what makes the expensive candidates
# measurable at all. Uncomment as a block, add your key above:
#
#   OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   BRAIN_LLM=openrouter
#   BRAIN_TRANSCRIBER=openrouter
#   BRAIN_URL_SAFETY=off          # unless you have a Safe Browsing key
#   RAGLAB_LLM=ollama
#
# BRAIN_MODEL and RAGLAB_MODEL are deliberately absent from that block: the
# providers above already resolve to `openai/gpt-5-nano` and
# `4skl/gemma4-e2b-mtp` through PROVIDER_MODELS, so naming them again only
# creates a second place to keep in sync.
#
# Note on BRAIN_OMNI_MODEL with BRAIN_TRANSCRIBER=openrouter: leave it at the
# default. `openai/whisper-*` does not work here — measured 2026-07-31,
# OpenRouter's catalogue holds no whisper entry at all, so dictation fails
# outright (see the note above `omni_model` in `config.py`).
